\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces CATCH training and inference. A Haar transform maps the voided image to eight subbands; these are concatenated with the noisy target subbands and a signed mask. The WavUNet predicts clean coefficients. After ancestral DDPM sampling, the inverse transform and hard compositing restore the observed region exactly. Thumbnails are illustrative and were selected without reconstruction metrics.}}{3}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:catch-architecture}{{1}{3}{CATCH training and inference. A Haar transform maps the voided image to eight subbands; these are concatenated with the noisy target subbands and a signed mask. The WavUNet predicts clean coefficients. After ancestral DDPM sampling, the inverse transform and hard compositing restore the observed region exactly. Thumbnails are illustrative and were selected without reconstruction metrics}{figure.1}{}}
